      "calculationScope": "EXACT_MANUAL_CALCULATION",
      "manualArithmetic": "All source tasks are symbolic relations and direction reasoning. In right-handed xright,yup,zout coordinates, k cross i=j gives outgoing-wire field upward at its right; i cross(-k)=j gives the positive-particle upward force, reversed for negative charge. Dotting q(v cross B) withv giveszero power. Classical qabs*vperp*B=m*vperp²/r yields r=m*vperp/(qabs*B). Exact sine/cosine parametrization differentiates to the Lorentz equation and constant vperp²+vparallel², with unchanged axialvelocity; helical radius usesvperp, notfullspeed. The wire derivation sums n*Across*length carriers each withqabs*vd*B and usesI=n*qabs*vd*Across. Constructed manual unit probes2C*3m/s*4T=24N;2kg*3m/s/(1C*2T)=3m;2A*3m*4T=24N. No assigned numerical charge/mass or numerical trigonometry appears.",
      "manualFeasibility": "PASS_AI_EXACT",
      "physicalAssumptions": "Right-handed coordinates; conventionalcurrent andsignedq. Longstraightwireawayfromends forcirculartangent fielddescription. Magneticforceonly whenstatingzero magneticwork; absenceofotherforces andspatiallyuniformB fororbitalmodel. Classicalnonrelativisticconstantmass mechanics,nonzerocharge/B,positive transverse speed fornondegeneratefinitecircle. Forinclinedvelocity radius usestransversecomponent, parallelcomponentadvancesunchanged. Straightwiresegment,uniformB andconventionalcurrentvectorlength; sin angle taken0..pi.",
      "pedagogicalReview": "Introducescurrent/compassdirection,charge signandcrossproduct beforecircularmodel. Explicitvparallel zero-force andperpendicularcondition avoidusingfullspeed forhelicalradius; no claim magneticforceadds kineticenergy. Wirelength followsconventionalcurrent, ratherthanelectrondrift.",
